abstract: >-
  Reproducible code, internal pre-specification protocol, deviation log, and
  derived datasets for a two-phase study of Inka khipus across OKR v2.1.0
  (n = 611) and disjoint KFG-only Excel workbooks (n = 36). Phase 1 reports
  internally pre-specified inter-archive invariance controlling for column count
  and sample size (primary modal color match and OKR numeric rank plus JSD
  robustness), explicit tabular outlier accounting (21/86), and a null result
  (0/30 BH-FDR) against five highland Textos Andinos schemas calibrated with
  FDR and nominal power plus proxy controls. Phase 2 (exploratory) documents
  five candidate hierarchical regularities of subsidiary cords evaluated at the
  khipu level (including a vertical spacing dose-response contrast and blind KFG
  out-of-sample replication), regional archive variation across eight sites, and
  a descriptive 611 x 611 rare-number sweep (538 filtered pairs) surfacing a
  putative three-khipu Berlin split-ledger link (VA 42518 <-> VA 63038 b /
  VA 63038(B)) and a putative reversed physical duplicate (VA 24370(B) <->
  VA 66834), both pending museum verification.
